<p>This street scene, taken in Cork in 1927, seems to give a 3-D effect, but it&#8217;s only alternating between two photos taken from slightly different perspectives. The sense of depth comes from parallax and the occlusion of distant objects.</p>
<p>Small animals bob their heads to produce this effect as they plan a jump; it helps them to estimate distance.</p>
